BT 1 0 0 1 0 172.5 Tm 14 TL /F1 9.5 Tf 0 0 0 rg (1. Start the program and initialize current_text as an empty string.) Tj  T* (2. Display the menu and read the user's choice.) Tj  T* (3. If choice is 1, clean whitespace in entered text.) Tj  T* (4. If choice is 2, normalize text according to the user's options.) Tj  T* (5. If choice is 3, count characters and words.) Tj  T* (6. If choice is 4, search for a phrase and show matching positions.) Tj  T* (7. If choice is 5, extract the requested slice.) Tj  T* (8. If choice is 6, compare two strings.) Tj  T* (9. If choice is 7 or 8, load from or save to a UTF-8 file.) Tj  T* (10. If choice is 9, display current text.) Tj  T* (11. If choice is 0, display the exit message and stop.) Tj  T* (12. If input or file processing fails, display an error and return to the menu.) Tj  T* (13. Repeat until the user exits.) Tj T* ET
Q
